WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.608
This module presents four case studies: hiring for an all-male AI team,

2
00:00:07.608 --> 00:00:12.411
recruiting diverse participants in a clinical trial, power and credit in a

3
00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:16.760
social science group, and opening up an undergraduate research lab.

4
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.793
The first lesson is to widen the search.

5
00:00:20.143 --> 00:00:23.242
Narrow channels, like a single bulletin board or an

6
00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:26.585
elite network, produce narrow teams and narrow samples.

7
00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:29.810
The second is to make criteria explicit.

8
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.667
Transparent criteria for hiring, workload and authorship reduce bias based on rank or identity.

9
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.995
The third is to share power.

10
00:00:39.345 --> 00:00:44.316
Inclusion means real voice, credit and leadership, not only being present in the room.

11
00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:47.135
And the fourth is to measure and adjust.

12
00:00:47.485 --> 00:00:50.769
Track outcomes over time, and treat DEI efforts as

13
00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:54.184
integral to good research, not as an optional extra.

